  "abstractText": "Hidden boron catalysis plagues catalyzed hydroboration reactions, with the \"catalyst\" acting to mediate the decomposition of HBpin/HBcat to BH<sub>3</sub> which is the actual (hidden) catalyst. <i>N</i>,<i>N</i>,<i>N'</i>,<i>N</i>'-Tetramethylethylenediamine (TMEDA) has been used to identify hidden boron catalysis through trapping/inhibition. Kinetic analyses showed that TMEDA inhibition is only applicable below 60 °C and that other amine traps are likewise ineffective. Awareness of this temperature limitation reveals widespread hidden catalysis in previous methods and should limit future false negative tests.",
